{
  "description": "#6741 — `change_property_type` turns a key into one that holds a list, and back. `people` (text): `X` \"Ann, Bob ,, Cy\", `Y` \"Solo\", `Z` \" , \". Split at commas, each text becomes the list of its trimmed parts, blanks dropped; `Z` has no part and is kept as it is, unfit (#6206); the undo puts the texts and the single-value definition back. `authors` (a list of text) stops holding a list, joined with semicolons: `X`'s two items become one text, `Y`'s one item its text. `scores` (a list of numbers) stops holding a list, joined with commas, which only a text or a URL takes: `Y`'s one item becomes its number, `X`'s two are kept as the list, which doesn't fit. Refused: a list of booleans, and a change of neither the type nor the flag. Last, a `related` list of refs written by a page's `[[Title]]` holds that page. The previews show a list as its line of text (`write_property_list`), so a list of one item holding a comma is quoted. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
